   "selectedScalarCauseLimitation": "STATED LIMITATION, not a defect to be engineered around. input-closure-incomplete retains ONE NativeCause while several missing inputs may coexist. Provenance of the selection: the producer names the cause it acted on, and Run closure checks that the named cause is lawful for the deficiency - it does not and cannot enumerate the inputs that were not named. What IS fully retained beside it is the rest of the Coverage entry and the Run's own evidence: the missing dependency sources, prepared rows and generated files are retained records in their own right, so a consumer that needs the complete set reads those rather than the scalar. No multi-cause format is introduced merely to make the prose true; the bounded source/ownership laws stay exactly as they are, and the limitation is published so no consumer reads the scalar as exhaustive.",
